-ART350&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-C</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rubin</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Adler</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Fowlkes</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Spratt</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Pallister</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Carson</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fractional moving blood volume: estimation with power Doppler US</article-title><source>Radiology</source><year>1995</year><volume>197</volume><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>190</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7568820</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bude</surname><given-names>RO</given-names></name><name><surname>Rubin</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Power Doppler sonography</article-title><source>Radiology</source><year>1996</year><volume>200</volume><fpage>21</fpage><lpage>23</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8657912</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Walther</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Harms</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Krenn</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Radke</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Faehndrich</surname><given-names>TP</given-names></name><name><surname>Gohlke</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Correlation of power Doppler sonography with vascularity of the synovial tissue of the knee joint in patients with osteoarthritis and rheumatoid arthritis</ar